A||||2||saleenfiero||What the??? (Asuna related)||||1||
Z||000000||saleenfiero||09-04-2001||06:03 PM||||Kay, I was driving today and we pull up next to an Asuna Sunfire(anyone remember those).  Did Pontiac do these things?  I'm sure I could see a little factory badge on the car that said "Handling by Lotus".  Did Lotus have anything to do with these cars or is it just like in the case of the fiero's Lotus handling?||||reg||1
Z||000001||RRobinson||09-04-2001||06:56 PM||||Asuna was created by GM Canada as a brand under which to sell domestically badged imports (the same as the now also defunct Geo). In Canada, GM dealerships were (and are) almost always Pontiac-Buick-GMC or Chevrolet-Oldsmobile-Cadillac-Geo. In 1993, GM created Asuna, probably because the P-B-G dealerships were bitching about the C-O-P dealerships getting Geo. Anyways, it must have been a bust, because Asuna lasted one whole year, '93.<P>Hardware? As far as I can remember,<BR>Isuzu Impulse=Geo Storm=Asuna Sunfire<BR>Except for badges, the Sunfire was a EXACT copy of the impulse, down to the "Handling by Lotus" badges.<BR>Geo Tracker=Asuna Sunrunner(ugh)<P>Thats all I can remember right now,<P>RR<BR>2-88 GTs<BR>2-87 GTs<BR>87 SE V6<BR>86 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||RRobinson||09-04-2001||07:00 PM||||...and yes, I believe that Lotus had enough to do with the suspension development to warrant the badges...unlike Fieros.<BR>RR||||reg||1
